u  kept saying Abby you know stress does  not impact your your outcomes here your  chances of getting pregnant probably  telling me that as a way to make me feel  less stressed but I still inherently  just knew instinctively that my stress  and my lack of sleep was obviously not  helping the cause so I really made an  extra effort especially this last  transfer round to to get my stress and  sleep under control and I obviously made  a whole video about some of these  strategies that helped my insomnia so  you can check that out right here but  some of the things I was doing included  taking on you know not working  or really even doing any screen time  before bed taking on fewer projects  taking more downtime and also ultimately  doing a lot of therapy and then finally  gentle exercise so for this cycle I  really did try to tone down my exercise  regime  I stopped any cardio I dropped my  weights down that I was using so let's  say I was bench pressing like 25 pounds  I took it down to like 15 which was  really hard for me at first because I  was like this is so easy and boring and  I got like getting anything out of this  but it was still really nice to move my  body now I'm probably doing like 20  pounds and I'll stay here for the rest  of my pregnancy not expecting or wanting  to like get stronger or anything like  that and then I'll pick it up when I  feel ready postpartum but I really  didn't want to get my heart rate up too  high and I also did not want to spike my  cortisol as high cortisol has been  associated with infertility so there's  that - okay so let's talk about diet  here now there are a bunch of like  Chinese medicine recommendations for  fertility especially with like thin  uterine lining so people are  recommending me to eat lots of red foods  because it helps with blood flow but  honestly I didn't find any research to  back any of these things up so I didn't  want to stress myself out unnecessarily  by like making all I can elite red foods  so the only thing I really did  concentrate on for the most part was no  caffeine I didn't even have chocolate I  also cut out alcohol actually for this  last cycle but not even yeah not even  any chocolate like maybe a bike here  there but really not much more than that  and a lot of women out there can have  chocolate I mean not just talked about  any caffeine without any issues in early  pregnancy but there is evidence to  suggest that having more than 200  milligrams is associated with double the  miscarriage risk and for someone who was  already clearly prone to that I was not  willing to take that risk  also one of the drugs I'm on prednisone  causes eggs  and insomnia and I really did not want  to perpetuate those side effects the  other thing that I I guess I really was  concentrating on was just eating enough  food because again I didn't want to  spike my cortisol and under fueling is  something that can is linked to to  higher levels of cortisol so for me I  was just really focusing on lots of  healthy snacks lots of healthy fats at  all my meals and just lots of nourishing  comfort foods okay so now let's get into  the hard stuff my drugs okay so first of  all is the estrogen patches and  injections so most people will have to  do either patches or estrogen  suppositories vaginal suppositories is a  way to help thicken the uterine lining  and because my uterine lining was so  temperamental I also had to do  injections this transfer round which I  had never done before I had always just  done either patches or suppositories and  clearly it really didn't do that much so  we added in those injections and that  seemed to help progesterone is another  thing that really is a non-negotiable  for IVF so you do suppositories so I did  those three times today and then  injections every other day and the  injections are in the old bum thank you  to my nurse husband for doing that every  morning for me but basically you start  the progesterone what you're lining  reaches the desired thickness and it  really just helps to kind of like  stabilize the lining and prevent  pregnancy loss so in fact some women  even if they're not undergoing IVF will  take progesterone in the first trimester  just as a way to kind of stabilize  things and keep things nice and steady  and good okay  next was vaginal viagra yes you heard me  right I remember when I went to the  pharmacy one time to pick this up and  the pharmacist was like sorry ma'am I  hate to do this but like can you tell me  what this is for exactly I've never seen  instructions to give viagra vaginally as  a suppository and of course I explained  it to him but basically viagra  increases blood flow to the nether  regions and since a uterine lining  requires good blood flow the theory is  that the viagra's if given vaginally as  the suppositories is going to help with  that blood flow and thicken the uterine  lining and actually there is some pretty  good evidence that it does work for some  women now I will say that my my cycle  before this one which was like super  long and drawn out  it used vaginal viagra and it did not  work for me but it who knows what  exactly went wrong but one thing I  figured out in retrospect was that with  the failed cycle I just went to the  regular pharmacy and got the  prescription filled there and they gave  me just the regular stereotypical blue  pills that men usually take and I just  feel like they were never actually  dissolving and absorbing properly this  is gonna be a total TMI but basically  everything all the time I would insert  to one of these blue pills vaginally I  would like feel up there a bunch of  undissolved pills and I was like am i  spending like $100 a day on this drug  and it's not even absorbing or  dissolving then with this cycle that  actually did work I went to the  compounding pharmacy and they had  actually compounded me proper vaginal  suppositories that were like clear and  they dissolved and it was like super  easy and I mean that wouldn't ended up  working so I don't know just a little  pro tip tip if you get prescribed  vaginal viagra for infertility or thin  uterine lining I don't know maybe try to  go to a compounding pharmacy to get an  actual suppository okay next was  low-dose aspirin  so aspirin is a vasodilator so it  increases blood flow to the uterus which  in turn can help thicken theater and  lining and there is research to suggest  that adding low-dose aspirin to your  protocol may help to thicken the up the  lining and also increase pregnancy rates  so that was something that we had in my  protocol pretty much from the beginning  once we realized that the line was an  issue  and then finally I took the  antihistamine CPP a protocol so this  protocol requires you to take ten  milligrams of prednisone ten milligrams  of claritin and 20 milligrams of pepcid  every single day and the theory is that  one of the reasons why we see recurrent  miscarriage is that the the uterus is  natural killer cells attack the foreign  fetus and so these drugs actually down  regulate the immune system in the hopes  that the fetus will be spared now there  is some medium quality evidence to  suggest that this protocol does work and  a lot of fertility clinics do say  anecdotally that it works for a lot of  women so that's why we decided to give  it a go  however I will say it's not easy it was  my least favorite drug to have to take  prednisone is evil and I mean ten  milligrams is not even a super high dose  so I have I can't even imagine having to  take a clinical like like IBD type of  dose like 50 or 60 milligrams because 10  milligrams alone made me feel super  loopy and bloated and just kind of crazy  also super anxious so hated that but  again kitchen sink approach I was  willing to do anything okay so finally  let's talk about the procedures that  helped me get pregnant so first of all  obviously IVF we did IVF with XE and PGS  testing for this round and XE is  basically where unlike