 magic procedure that we all believed was  what got me pregnant this is what made  all of the difference so I remember my  doctor sitting me down and being like  Abby are you ready to go into like  uncharted like non evidence-based  territory with me and I was like yes I  am desperate take me there I will do  anything at this point and he explained  to me that in his clinical experience a  lot of women who've been on the pill for  a very long period of time were  breastfed for a long period of time  their estrogen is so levels are  suppressed but their uterus kind of like  curtains up and shrivels up I mean I'm  sure that's not the actual technical  process of what actually is going on but  that was how he's trying to explain to  it to me in mid and like laypersons  terms basically and so he likened it to  having like a thin eggshell coating  around the uterus that made it very  difficult if not impossible for any  estrogen including the the kind of  synthetic estrogen that they were giving  me as drugs to penetrate the uterus to  thickened the uterine lining so he was  thinking about this experience as you  know those days where you have a muscle  knot and you go in there for her deep  tissue massage and they're really  massaging in there to try to get the  blood flow back to the to the muscle and  he thought hmm what if I could massage  the uterus to help stimulate blood flow  and therefore thicken the uterine lining  well he obviously wasn't going to stick  his whole hand in me and manually  massage my uterus so what he did instead  or his his theory was I can put a  balloon up into your uterus and pump the  balloon up and essentially break that  shell and then of course you'd go on to  have a normal typical transfer cycle  taking estrogen to thicken the lining  but without any research having been  done on this this procedure of course  this is just something he made up he had  done this on eight other women all of  which had very similar stories that I  had so 